{"text": "Imagine a New Law That Could\nMake Your Life Easier\n\nH.B. 299 may be the answer\nOhio tobacco retailers are looking for\n\nH.B. 299 would finally rein in the numerous UNELECTED health board\nbureaucrats who are hell-bent on imposing as many burdensome and duplicative\nregulations as possible on tobacco retailers and the state\u2019s hospitality industry.\n\nH.B, 299 provides for uniform, statewide laws regulating the marketing and\nsales of tobacco products, regardless of the store location.\n\nH.B, 299 recognizes that education is a key to preventing the sale of cigarettes\nto minors. All retail clerks would be required to sign a form acknowledging that\nthey are aware of the state\u2019s minimum age laws, similar to the form found in\nthe Philip Morris \"Ask First/It\u2019s The Law\u201d kit sent to you earlier this year.\n\nH.B. 299 allows a juvenile court to impose fines or community service when a\nminor is convicted of purchasing tobacco products.\n\nH.B, 299 allows for federally required, unannounced monitoring of retailers;\nhowever, only law enforcement officials can issue citations to retailers caught\nselling tobacco to minors.\n\nH.B. 299 prohibits the sale of single cigarettes and other tobacco products in\nopened packages.\n\nBut H.B. 299 Won\u2019t Become Law Without Your Help!\n\nPlease take a few minutes TODAY and let your legislators know that you\nsupport H.B. 299, legislation to establish uniform statewide smoking\nregulations.\n\n\u201cFESEGSLEOG",
